From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:53:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Keep the Beacon events of an AP MLD while a link beacons

wpa_driver_nl80211_del_beacon() drops the reference of the interface to
the Beacon event subscription of the wiphy whenever one link stops
beaconing. If no other BSS of the same driver instance holds a
reference, the other links of an AP MLD lose the OBSS Beacon events
that feed OLBC detection and the AP list. A link that keeps beaconing
does not take the reference again.

Drop the reference only when no link of the interface beacons.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -3628,6 +3628,21 @@ wpa_driver_nl80211_finish_drv_init(struc
 }
 
 
+static bool nl80211_bss_beaconing(struct i802_bss *bss)
+{
+	int link_id;
+
+	if (!bss->valid_links)
+		return bss->flink->beacon_set;
+
+	for_each_link(bss->valid_links, link_id)
+		if (bss->links[link_id].beacon_set)
+			return true;
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
 static int wpa_driver_nl80211_del_beacon(struct i802_bss *bss,
 					 int link_id)
 {
@@ -3643,7 +3658,11 @@ static int wpa_driver_nl80211_del_beacon
 	link->beacon_set = 0;
 	link->freq = 0;
 
-	nl80211_put_wiphy_data_ap(bss);
+	/* The Beacon event subscription is the interface's, and the other
+	 * links of an AP MLD still feed OLBC detection and the AP list with
+	 * the Beacons it delivers. */
+	if (!nl80211_bss_beaconing(bss))
+		nl80211_put_wiphy_data_ap(bss);
 	msg = nl80211_bss_msg(bss, 0, NL80211_CMD_DEL_BEACON);
 	if (!msg)
 		return -ENOBUFS;
